#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "provisioning.security"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Product Bundle Worker Permissions
	Testing to assure that provisioning product bundle worker permissions works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I create a provisioning user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | provisioning.worker                    |
	| Email Address | provisioning.worker@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Provisioning                           |
	| Last Name     | Worker                                 |
	* I assign the provisioning user with the email address "provisioning.worker@liferay.com.broken" to the provisioning role "Provisioning Worker"

Teardown:
	* I log out and log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "nHZMPLWyzvRKujPLqfHK"
	* I go to the product bundles index page
	* I tear down the following product bundles
	| Visible Products |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Visible Product        |
	| A Visible Second Product |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from provisioning
	| provisioning.worker@liferay.com.broken |

Scenario: View no new product bundle button
	Testing the inability to create product bundles in the provisioning product index 

	Given I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.worker@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the product bundles index page
	And the new product bundle button should not be present

Scenario: View product bundle
	Testing the ability to view product bundles in the provisioning product index that do not contain a link or delete button

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Visible Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Visible Second Product | |
	And I log out and log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "nHZMPLWyzvRKujPLqfHK"
	And I go to the product bundles index page
	And I click on the new product bundle button
	And I populate and save the product bundle form with the following values
	| Name        | Input | Visible Products         |
	| Add Product |       | A Visible Product        |
	| Add Product |       | A Visible Second Product |
	And I log out and log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.worker@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the product bundles index page
	Then I should be able to view a non linked product bundle on the provisioning index with the name "Visible Products" and the following values
	| Name | Visible Products |
	And the delete button for the product bundle "Visible Products" should not be present